Version 2.3.0 (2026/07/29)
* Redesigned the PC settings panel to use a dropdown selector instead of
  individual collapsible control panels for each ability; this significantly
  reduces the total number of controls that need to be created for the settings
  panel and should eliminate the brief lag that is encountered when opening the
  settings panel for the first time

Version 2.2.1 (2026/07/15)
* Expanded the conditional enablement for Major Courage to include the Ferocious
  Roar ability

Version 2.2.0 (2026/07/13)
* Added a Placement Preview Mode to temporarily expand panel sizes to either 12
  or 4 players and bypass group, zone, and conditional enablement requirements;
  this feature can be accessed via the settings panel

Version 2.1.2 (2026/06/09)
* Improved compatibility for Xbox on PC

Version 2.1.1 (2026/05/21)
* By user request, added support for Arkay's Charity cooldown; this entails
  inclusion in the default Supported Effects list, support for conditional
  enablement, and an icon override
* Adjusted the console settings panel in response to recent changes in
  LibHarvensAddonSettings

Version 2.1.0 (2026/03/10)
* It is now possible to track effects that use multiple ability IDs; additional
  IDs are delimited by "+" in the Supported Effects list
* Added Standard of Might (32948+29230) to the default Supported Effects list
  - This should track both Standard of Might and the base Dragonknight Standard
  - If you have not altered the Supported Effects list, you should see this
    change automatically, otherwise you will have to either make this change
    manually or reset your Supported Effects list back to default

Version 2.0.3 (2026/02/24)
* The Supported Effects List can now be edited on console

Version 2.0.2 (2025/11/02)
* Added French localization by Melicious

Version 2.0.1 (2025/09/13)
* Fixed a bug with configuring panel-specific scaling on console

Version 2.0.0 (2025/09/11)
* Group Buff Panels now supports settings profiles, to allow players to quickly
  swap between different panel layouts and configurations
  - Character-specific settings from version 1.x will be seamlessly converted
    into profiles under this new system
  - There is an API for the new profiles system, so external third-party addons
    can potentially change profiles, e.g., swap to a profile in response to the
    player loading a certain setup
* Added console support
* Added a scaling option to change the overall size of the panels
* Changed the ID for Major Berserk from 62195 to 61745 in the default Supported
  Effects list

Version 1.2.1 (2025/09/02)
* Added new "Mark dead players with strikethrough text" setting so that it is
  easier to see the reason why a dead player is not receiving buffs

Version 1.2.0 (2025/08/26)
* It is now possible to track effects that do not trigger EVENT_EFFECT_CHANGED
  by instead using EVENT_COMBAT_EVENT; to flag an effect for this alternate
  tracking method, make its ability ID negative in the Supported Effects list
* The default Supported Effects list has been changed to replace 172055
  (Pillager's Profit ulti gen) with -172056 (Pillager's Profit cooldown, using
  alternate tracking)
  - If you have not altered the Supported Effects list, you should see this
    change automatically, otherwise you will have to either make this change
    manually or reset your Supported Effects list back to default
  - Since panel settings are associated with the ability ID of the effect, this
    unfortunately means that any configuration changes made to the 172055 panel
    will not carry over to the new 172056 panel

Version 1.1.0 (2025/08/25)
* Added new "Snap position" setting to ease the process of aligning multiple
  panels with each other
* Added new "Hide header icon and caption" setting for players who prefer to
  memorize what each panel does solely by their positions
* Added conditional enablement options for Major Slayer/Aegis, Major Courage,
  Major Resolve, Radiating Regeneration, Echoing Vigor, and Aggressive Horn

Version 1.0.0 (2025/08/23)
* Initial version
